  data: {
    LLM: "If you hold the 10 or 5 of trumps, do not lead them! Wait until a higher trump (Ace or King) has been played so you can safely drop them on a winning trick.\n\nBegging is more common in All Fives than All Fours because you need a high-point trump suit to score effectively. If the turned-up trump is a suit you are short in, always beg.\n\nDefensive Trumping: If an opponent leads a high non-trump suit (e.g., Ace of Spades) and you suspect they have the point-trumps, trump early to 'steal' the lead and force them to play their trumps out of order.",
    Player: "If you hold the 10 or 5 of trumps, do not lead them! Wait until a higher trump (Ace or King) has been played so you can safely drop them on a winning trick.\n\nBegging is more common in All Fives than All Fours because you need a high-point trump suit to score effectively. If the turned-up trump is a suit you are short in, always beg.\n\nDefensive Trumping: If an opponent leads a high non-trump suit (e.g., Ace of Spades) and you suspect they have the point-trumps, trump early to 'steal' the lead and force them to play their trumps out of order.",
